# Era 3 — Mental Model & Setup (V6–V9)

_Phase 2 · Concept Layer V1_

**Status: ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17**

**Implementation note:** `concepts/how-beaver-fits-together.mdx` (V6, new — the canonical
diagram/vocabulary every later page reuses) and `concepts/accounts-and-workspaces.mdx` (V9,
new) written. V7 (Choosing my setup) and V8 (Installation/CLI basics) executed as merges per
Era 1's classification — `choose-your-setup.mdx` gained a "what you supply, what Beaver
manages" note; `installation.mdx` gained a "Staying up to date" section (version
compatibility, `beaver update`). One real bug found during review: several later-era pages
initially linked to `/concepts/choosing-my-setup` and `/concepts/connecting-machines` as if
they were new pages — wrong, since V7/T2 and Era 4 V11/T6 are merges with no page of their
own. Fixed by pointing every such link at the real merge target (`/choose-your-setup`,
`/connect`) instead. `mint broken-links` clean.

Covers T1–T4 (`concepts-explained.txt`'s "How Beaver fits together," "Choosing my setup,"
"Installation and CLI basics," "Accounts and workspaces"). V6 is the single highest-leverage
version in the roadmap: it fixes the one entity diagram and vocabulary every later concept
page's "how this relates" section reuses (Invariant 8).

---

## V6 — How Beaver fits together (T1)

### Goal
One new concept page giving the product-level mental model: workspace → project →
environment → machine/cloud → deployment → container → service, and how they relate.

### Reuses
Nothing existing — no page currently does this at the entity-relationship level; `features.mdx`
lists features but doesn't relate them. This is genuinely net-new (V2's classification:
`new-page`).

### Implement
- `concepts/how-beaver-fits-together.mdx` using the Era 2 template.
- One diagram (entities + relationship arrows only, per `DISCLOSURE-ADDENDUM.md`'s system
  diagram rule) — built from an existing Mintlify-supported approach (a described flow using
  `<Steps>`/`<Card>` layout, or an embedded image under `images/`, whichever the actual
  drafting session finds renders cleanest; no new component).
- Defines the vocabulary every later page's relationship section links back to: this page
  becomes the canonical link target for "see how this fits into the bigger picture."

### Validate
- Every entity named in the diagram maps to a real product concept from the T1–T34 list, so
  no later page introduces a relationship this diagram doesn't already show.
- Passes `DISCLOSURE-ADDENDUM.md` review — no placement/scheduling arrows.

### Done when
The page exists and is confirmed as the one diagram every later era's "relates to" section
links to, rather than each page drawing its own.

---

## V7 — Choosing my setup (T2)

### Goal
Resolve the `merge-into-choose-your-setup` classification from Era 1 V2: keep the existing
onboarding narrative in `Getting started`, but ensure it now answers T2's full scope (single
machine vs. cloud, laptop viability, machine roles, prerequisites, what infrastructure the
user supplies) and links forward into the new Concepts group for depth it doesn't need to
carry itself.

### Reuses
`choose-your-setup.mdx` as-is; extends rather than forks it (Invariant 9).

### Implement
- Gap-check `choose-your-setup.mdx` against T2's five sub-points; add only what's missing.
- Add a forward link from `choose-your-setup.mdx` into `how-beaver-fits-together.mdx` (V6)
  and into `machine-roles.mdx`/`connect.mdx` where the onboarding narrative currently
  under-explains a concept it references in passing.

### Validate
- No new standalone page created for T2 (per the V2 classification) unless the gap-check
  finds the existing narrative structurally can't hold the missing content without becoming
  a reference page itself — if so, escalate and log the deviation here rather than silently
  splitting.

### Done when
`choose-your-setup.mdx` answers T2 completely and links into the new mental-model page.

---

## V8 — Installation and CLI basics (T3)

### Goal
Same merge pattern as V7, targeting `installation.mdx` / `installation-windows.mdx` /
`beaver-doctor.mdx` / `cli.mdx`.

### Reuses
The four existing pages; the sibling roadmap's `cli.mdx` (its own "Overview" page in the CLI
tab) for what it already covers about interactive shell vs. terminal commands, help, and
completion, so this version doesn't re-explain flag-level material that belongs there.

### Implement
- Confirm platform coverage, update/version-compatibility explanation, and
  interactive-vs-terminal distinction are present at the concept level across these pages;
  add what's missing.
- This is the one T# where the existing reference page (`cli.mdx`) already partially
  overlaps a "concept" role — resolve by keeping `cli.mdx` as the CLI tab's overview
  (syntax-adjacent) and any conceptual "why use the interactive shell" framing in
  `installation.mdx` or a short new section there, not duplicated in both.

### Validate
- No content contradicts between `cli.mdx` and whichever Getting-Started page ends up
  carrying the conceptual framing.

### Done when
A reader gets a complete "how do I install and use the CLI at all" story without needing
the CLI tab's reference pages first.

---

## V9 — Accounts and workspaces (T4)

### Goal
A new concept page: login/logout/whoami as account identity, workspace as the scoping unit,
what deleting or recreating a workspace means.

### Reuses
`cli/login.mdx`/`cli/logout.mdx`/`cli/whoami.mdx` (or the sibling roadmap's Era 3 `auth`
family page, whichever exists by the time this version runs) as the reference-layer link
target; nothing existing covers this at concept level.

### Implement
- `concepts/accounts-and-workspaces.mdx` using the Era 2 template.
- Prerequisites section: none (this is typically the first concept a new user needs).
- Relationship section links to `how-beaver-fits-together.mdx` (workspace sits above
  project) and forward to `choose-your-setup.mdx`.
- Consequences section states workspace deletion/recreation effects at the observable level
  (what becomes inaccessible, what is not recoverable) without describing storage internals.

### Validate
- Passes disclosure review; links resolve (reference page may be a placeholder if the
  sibling roadmap's `auth` family isn't written yet — noted honestly, per that roadmap's own
  Invariant 9 marking convention, not left silently broken).

### Done when
Page exists, is placed in the new Concepts group (pending Era 12 nav wiring), and closes
Era 3.
